#
# THE SCHWUNG EVERY MOVE MODULE HERE IS TESTED AGAINST -- one version, named
# once. modules/_shared/schwung.sh fetches exactly this into a cache and
# verifies it; the vendored host headers (engines/trance-gate/include) must be
# its headers byte for byte, and the editor's smoke test runs on its shared
# modules. Release tooling reads it too.
#
# FORMAT: KEY=VALUE lines, nothing else; `#` starts a comment line. No quotes,
# no spaces around `=`, no expansion -- read it with a line split on the first
# `=`, or source it from a POSIX shell.
#
#   SCHWUNG_REPO    the GitHub owner/repo the version is fetched from
#   SCHWUNG_TAG     its release tag
#   SCHWUNG_COMMIT  the full commit SHA that tag named when it was pinned.
#                   The fetch fails if the tag names anything else now: a
#                   moved tag is a different Schwung under the same name.
#
# TO MOVE IT: set all three, run `modules/_shared/schwung.sh headers`, vendor
# the headers it reports as different, and run the quick tier.
SCHWUNG_REPO=charlesvestal/schwung
SCHWUNG_TAG=v1.7.3
SCHWUNG_COMMIT=a6f7ec9e5cf4d0df172a1dbc00b29d0b5eb67124
